Unsloth: torchao==0.18.0 uses torch.float4_e2m1fn_x2, and the installed torch==2.7.0+cu118 does not have it, so this environment pairs a torchao with a torch that cannot serve it.
torch.float4_e2m1fn_x2 first appears in torch 2.7.0, so this torch is the older half.

Upgrade torch, which leaves torchao where it is:
    pip install --upgrade "torch>=2.7.0" "torchvision"
    That takes the default build from PyPI. This torch is a cu118 build, and each https://download.pytorch.org/whl/ index carries only the releases built for it, so pick the CUDA index for the release you are moving to at https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/ and pass it as --index-url.

Installing a torchao that matches this torch works too. Pip allowed the pair because torchao declares a lower torch floor than its own modules actually touch, so there was nothing for the resolver to reject.
